# Invariant 9's recovery and R25: a member that has fallen out of the epoch returns to the
# instance's head by an own-leaf external commit (POST /resync), and that resync is EXEMPT from
# invariant 5's freeze - making the one device that cannot act wait on a membership commit would
# deadlock it. Bob misses two epochs, the instance's Remove of carol freezes the group, and bob
# still resyncs; the Remove is re-issued for the new epoch and alice commits it.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8d8 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
go_offline bob
commit alice
commit alice
kick alice carol
go_online bob
resync bob chat
sync alice
commit alice
send alice chat back at the head
expect_decrypts bob chat back at the head
